Write Python function validate_selection(features) under25lines source only. For every pair selected NEW Bio.SeqFeature objects (exclude existing supplied by caller), if both locations not None and same location.strand and same strand in (-1,1), compute sets occupiedbases and intersection. If nonempty and intersection/len(a)>=.8 and intersection/len(b)>=.8 raise ValueError('Selected annotations overlap at the same locus. Select one competing candidate before saving.'). Else returns None. Different strands allowed. Do not reject all small overlaps. No arbitrary IO/imports.
RESPONSE
```python
from Bio.SeqFeature import SeqFeature, Location
def validate_selection(features):
    for i in range(len(features)):
        for j in range(i+1, len(features)):
            a, b = features[i], features[j]
            if not (a.location and b.location): continue
            if a.location.strand != b.location.strand: continue
            if a.location.strand not in (-1, 1): continue
            set_a = set(range(a.location.start, a.location.end))
            set_b = set(range(b.location.start, b.location.end))
            inter = set_a & set_b
            if not inter: continue
            if len(inter)/len(set_a) < 0.8 or len(inter)/len(set_b) < 0.8: continue
            raise ValueError('Selected annotations overlap at the same locus. Select one competing candidate before saving.')
    return None
```